# Manual requests for the IntelliJ / VS Code HTTP client. The full, current list is in Swagger UI:
# http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html
@host = http://localhost:8080

### Teams
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams

### Engineers of one team, by name
GET {{host}}/api/v1/engineers?team=SRE&active=true

### Newest alerts (paged)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/alerts?page=0&size=20

### Alerts filtered by engineer, severity and date, oldest first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/alerts?engineerId=1&severity=P1&start=2016-01-01&end=2016-12-31&sort=triggeredAt,asc

### Paging history of one alert
GET {{host}}/api/v1/alerts/1/assignments

### On-call shifts
GET {{host}}/api/v1/oncall?start=2026-09-01&end=2026-09-30

### Fairness (2016 data needs an explicit window)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/scores/fairness?start=2016-01-01&end=2016-12-31

### Burnout
GET {{host}}/api/v1/scores/burnout?days=30

### Time of day
GET {{host}}/api/v1/scores/timeofday?days=30

### All scores for one engineer
GET {{host}}/api/v1/scores/engineers/1?days=90

### PagerDuty incidents (live, not stored)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/incidents?limit=25

### PagerDuty users
GET {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/users

### Sync incidents now
POST {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/sync

### Backfill a year of on-call shifts
POST {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/sync/oncalls?days=365

### Resolve an incident as a PagerDuty user
POST {{host}}/api/v1/pagerduty/resolve/INCIDENT_ID?email=engineer@example.com

### Webhook ping (unversioned path; real events need a valid X-PagerDuty-Signature)
POST {{host}}/api/webhook/pagerduty
Content-Type: application/json

{"event": {"event_type": "pagey.ping"}}
